\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  The ALETHIA closed loop. The analytic SMEFT oracle of Section~\ref {sec:theory} supplies a binned cross-section ratio at chosen $(\bm  {c}, m_{\ell \ell })$. The closed-form attention head of Section~\ref {sec:attention} consumes the context $(M_{\rm  ctx}, Y_{\rm  ctx})$ through a ridge solve in a learned feature map $\bm  {\psi }_\theta $ and emits a prediction with closed-form predictive variance; the inverse design matrix $\bm  {A}^{-1}$ is maintained by Sherman-Morrison rank-one updates at $\mathcal  {O}(D^2)$ per added observation. Three drift monitors (a DAS-CUSUM on standardised residuals, a Benjamini-Hochberg-corrected per-region binomial coverage test, and an Eckart-Young condition-number monitor on the design matrix) drive an aggregator that escalates to EPIG acquisition, with Cauchy-Schwarz on the $\bm  {A}^{-1}$ inner product rendering the information gain non-negative. The underlying $\bm  {\psi }_\theta $ weights are not touched at inference.}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:loop}{{1}{2}{The ALETHIA closed loop. The analytic SMEFT oracle of Section~\ref {sec:theory} supplies a binned cross-section ratio at chosen $(\bm {c}, \mll )$. The closed-form attention head of Section~\ref {sec:attention} consumes the context $(M_{\rm ctx}, Y_{\rm ctx})$ through a ridge solve in a learned feature map $\psib _\theta $ and emits a prediction with closed-form predictive variance; the inverse design matrix $\bm {A}^{-1}$ is maintained by Sherman-Morrison rank-one updates at $\mathcal {O}(D^2)$ per added observation. Three drift monitors (a DAS-CUSUM on standardised residuals, a Benjamini-Hochberg-corrected per-region binomial coverage test, and an Eckart-Young condition-number monitor on the design matrix) drive an aggregator that escalates to EPIG acquisition, with Cauchy-Schwarz on the $\bm {A}^{-1}$ inner product rendering the information gain non-negative. The underlying $\psib _\theta $ weights are not touched at inference}{figure.caption.1}{}}
