\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces  Per-region minimum BH-corrected $p$-value of the binomial coverage test through the $400$-cycle closed-loop run, on a logarithmic axis. Each sawtooth tooth is one conformal recalibration cycle: residuals accumulate against the rolling calibration window until the minimum $p$-value plunges below $\alpha = 0.05$ (dashed) and the calibrator refits at the next acquisition fire, resetting the statistic. The cadence of $\sim \!25$ cycles per tooth is set by the calibration window length. Acquisition fires occur every $3$ cycles (cool-down-limited) until the oracle budget exhausts at cycle $\sim \!300$; the post-budget tail at right shows the residual stream continuing to drift without further refit.}}{14}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:drift-events}{{5}{14}{Per-region minimum BH-corrected $p$-value of the binomial coverage test through the $400$-cycle closed-loop run, on a logarithmic axis. Each sawtooth tooth is one conformal recalibration cycle: residuals accumulate against the rolling calibration window until the minimum $p$-value plunges below $\alpha = 0.05$ (dashed) and the calibrator refits at the next acquisition fire, resetting the statistic. The cadence of $\sim \!25$ cycles per tooth is set by the calibration window length. Acquisition fires occur every $3$ cycles (cool-down-limited) until the oracle budget exhausts at cycle $\sim \!300$; the post-budget tail at right shows the residual stream continuing to drift without further refit}{figure.caption.10}{}}
