\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces  Multi-seed sweep on the angular observable at the stressed budget, four representative cells of the $1\,000$-chain closed-loop sweep. Solid bars (left axis): contraction ratio $\Sigma _{\tilde  c_2}^{\rm  post}/\Sigma _{\tilde  c_2}^{\rm  seed}$, lower is more contraction. Hatched bars (right axis): MLE error on $\tilde  c_2$, lower is closer to the truth. Dotted horizontals mark the random baseline on each axis. The parameter-space $\Delta H_a$ acquisition contracts the posterior most on every cell and produces the largest MLE error on every cell; the predictive and leverage modes over-acquire the high-leverage ridge and end up with contraction at or above random while still producing inflated MLE error. Numbers from \texttt  {experiments/al-phoenix-studies/output/stage\_c\_closed\_loop\_aggregate.json}.}}{17}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:al-contraction-mle}{{7}{17}{Multi-seed sweep on the angular observable at the stressed budget, four representative cells of the $1\,000$-chain closed-loop sweep. Solid bars (left axis): contraction ratio $\Sigma _{\tilde c_2}^{\rm post}/\Sigma _{\tilde c_2}^{\rm seed}$, lower is more contraction. Hatched bars (right axis): MLE error on $\tilde c_2$, lower is closer to the truth. Dotted horizontals mark the random baseline on each axis. The parameter-space $\Delta H_a$ acquisition contracts the posterior most on every cell and produces the largest MLE error on every cell; the predictive and leverage modes over-acquire the high-leverage ridge and end up with contraction at or above random while still producing inflated MLE error. Numbers from \texttt {experiments/al-phoenix-studies/output/stage\_c\_closed\_loop\_aggregate.json}}{figure.caption.15}{}}
