\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces  The learned feature map $\bm  {\psi }_\theta : \mathbb  {R} \to \mathbb  {R}^{16}$ on the SMEFT oracle, evaluated on a dense grid in $m_{\ell \ell }$ (left), and the fixed polynomial feature map $\bm  {\psi }(m) = \{1, \log (m/M_{\rm  ref}), \ldots  , \log ^4(m/M_{\rm  ref})\}$ (right). The learned columns include localised bumps and tail-emphasising shapes that the fixed basis cannot represent.}}{25}{figure.caption.25}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:psi-basis}{{9}{25}{The learned feature map $\psib _\theta : \mathbb {R} \to \mathbb {R}^{16}$ on the SMEFT oracle, evaluated on a dense grid in $\mll $ (left), and the fixed polynomial feature map $\psib (m) = \{1, \log (m/\Mref ), \ldots , \log ^4(m/\Mref )\}$ (right). The learned columns include localised bumps and tail-emphasising shapes that the fixed basis cannot represent}{figure.caption.25}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces  Foundation-model comparison on the SMEFT oracle, ordered descending by $M$--$Y$ alignment retention. ``Closed-form properties'' lists whether the architecture admits the four analytic properties used by the drift-monitored inference loop: predictive variance (PV), information gain (IG), Sherman-Morrison update (SM), and Eckart-Young condition-number sensitivity (EY). Alignment retention is $1 - \cos $ of the embedding before and after shuffling $Y_{\rm  ctx}$ within the context. Held-out median $R^2$ is on $50$ out-of-distribution scenarios; $C_{\rm  rec}$ is the joint $R^2$ of a linear probe onto the four Warsaw operators. The constraint-violating regressor consumes $\bm  {c}$ on the forward pass; its alignment and $c$-recoverability cells are undefined by construction. Numbers from \texttt  {experiments/full-chain-run/output/architecture\_comparison.json}.}}{25}{table.caption.27}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:arch-comparison}{{6}{25}{Foundation-model comparison on the SMEFT oracle, ordered descending by $M$--$Y$ alignment retention. ``Closed-form properties'' lists whether the architecture admits the four analytic properties used by the drift-monitored inference loop: predictive variance (PV), information gain (IG), Sherman-Morrison update (SM), and Eckart-Young condition-number sensitivity (EY). Alignment retention is $1 - \cos $ of the embedding before and after shuffling $Y_{\rm ctx}$ within the context. Held-out median $R^2$ is on $50$ out-of-distribution scenarios; $C_{\rm rec}$ is the joint $R^2$ of a linear probe onto the four Warsaw operators. The constraint-violating regressor consumes $\bm {c}$ on the forward pass; its alignment and $c$-recoverability cells are undefined by construction. Numbers from \texttt {experiments/full-chain-run/output/architecture\_comparison.json}}{table.caption.27}{}}
